            <ArticleTitle>The butterfly sign: an indicator of fluid within both the greater peritoneal cavity and the lesser omental bursa.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>161-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fluid accumulations present in the lesser omental bursa and the greater peritoneal cavity simultaneously outline a pattern resembling a butterfly. This &quot;butterfly sign&quot; can contribute to a more accurate diagnosis in evaluation of acute pancreatic processes and, more generally, acute abdominal syndromes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
